# Ops AI task closeout + publishing style

## When this applies

If the work came from Ops AI (`ops_ai_dev_tasks`, `/x8/ai-tasks`, a `cursor_prompt`, Operator Dev Requests, or an approved AI task), **close the loop on the server** before ending the turn.

## Closeout checklist (mandatory)

1. **Mark done** — `POST /api/admin/ai-tasks/{id}/done` with a short `note` (what shipped / what to verify). Use normal admin auth (login / existing session). **Never** forge JWTs or bypass 2FA.
2. **Assigner notify** — Done path must notify the operator who created the task (Telegram when linked). After backend deploy this is automatic in `mark_task_done`. If notify may have failed, say so explicitly.
3. **Tell the human who asked** — one short line: task `#N` closed, assigner notified (or why not).
4. **Backfill** — if asked to “разошли старые” / closeout historical tasks: call the backfill path for `approved`/`done` rows without `done_notified_at` (mark done if needed, then notify once). Do not spam duplicates.

## Report / notify formatting

Structure every done note and Telegram notify like this (Telegram HTML, allowed tags only):

- **Title:** `Ops AI · готово #N` + task title
- **What changed:** 3–6 short bullets
- **Check:** one smoke line if relevant
- **Link:** admin task URL when `PUBLIC_SITE_URL` is known

No walls of text. No emoji spam.

## News / buyer posts (when writing broadcasts or channel copy)

Always format well:

1. Bold headline
2. 1–2 short paragraphs
3. Benefit bullets
4. Clear CTA (link or next step)

Prefer one branded FocusPay sticker with the post when a pack is available. Use `sanitize_telegram_html` / only Telegram-safe tags (`<b>`, `<i>`, `<a>`, …).

## Out of scope reminders

- No auto-commit / auto-deploy unless the user explicitly asked.
- Backend/nginx/restart = production; need explicit OK unless the current task already approved that deploy.
